WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.971
(high pitched engine whirs)

00:00:03.971 --> 00:00:07.012
- If people could understand that

00:00:07.012 --> 00:00:09.498
this is akin to the scariest
thing you've ever done,

00:00:09.498 --> 00:00:11.583
then they'll start to understand why

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:13.358
we're so addicted to it.

00:00:13.358 --> 00:00:14.935
When I put the goggles on,

00:00:14.935 --> 00:00:18.688
the first thing I'm doing
is trying to calm down.

00:00:18.688 --> 00:00:20.746
(hip hop music)

00:00:20.746 --> 00:00:22.946
It totally puts you inside the drone.

00:00:22.946 --> 00:00:26.139
You just forget where you are.

00:00:26.139 --> 00:00:28.806
(hip hop music)

00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:33.159
(acoustic guitar picking)

00:00:33.159 --> 00:00:35.967
I'm Conrad Miller, also known as Furadi

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:37.607
and I'm a drone racer.

00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:41.066
(acoustic guitar picking)

00:00:41.066 --> 00:00:43.903
I started in September
2014 and that was like

00:00:43.903 --> 00:00:45.320
the ground floor.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.346
(hip hop beat)

00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:51.431
Of all the activities I've partaken in,

00:00:51.431 --> 00:00:54.033
motorcycles and flying drones

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:57.411
are on the same level
in terms of intensity.

00:00:57.411 --> 00:00:58.244
Wooh.

00:00:59.587 --> 00:01:00.897
It's cool when you have a hobby

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:02.546
and you can do it and you love it.

00:01:02.546 --> 00:01:04.240
But when you can share it with your kids,

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.497
that's just like what
it's all about I think.

00:01:07.497 --> 00:01:09.711
Okay so the props are good.

00:01:09.711 --> 00:01:14.270
Flying and racing with Sorell
has just been a pure joy.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:16.789
He's a good kid and he's a talented kid.

00:01:16.789 --> 00:01:19.640
And I think it comes
easy to any kid like that

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.484
because they don't feel the
pressure that adults do.

00:01:23.484 --> 00:01:26.392
Good landing (chuckles).

00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:27.971
- [Sorell] Comin' in hot.

00:01:27.971 --> 00:01:31.245
- This is harder than
anything else I've done

00:01:31.245 --> 00:01:34.381
and it's because when your nerves go,

00:01:34.381 --> 00:01:36.325
your fine motor skills go.

00:01:36.325 --> 00:01:38.205
Kids don't care, they're just having fun

00:01:38.205 --> 00:01:40.414
and they just learn much faster.

00:01:40.414 --> 00:01:42.189
(hip hop beat)

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:44.067
The course in L.A. is
at the Hawthorne Mall

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:44.900
which is abandoned.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.928
It's been abandoned
since the 80's I believe

00:01:46.928 --> 00:01:48.373
and it looks like a
place where you would go

00:01:48.373 --> 00:01:50.330
if there was a zombie apocalypse.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.913
(high pitched motors whiz)

00:01:55.318 --> 00:01:57.818
(racers cheer and applaud)

00:01:57.818 --> 00:01:59.542
When I go into races I feel like I put

00:01:59.542 --> 00:02:02.533
a lot of pressure on myself to win.

00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:04.950
I want all of my practice and

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:09.875
all of my time flying
to show for something.

00:02:09.875 --> 00:02:11.593
(motor whizzes and crashes)

00:02:11.593 --> 00:02:13.694
(crowd ooohs)

00:02:13.694 --> 00:02:16.028
I was flying fine, I wasn't nervous, but,

00:02:16.028 --> 00:02:18.384
I was just a little too high and crashed.

00:02:18.384 --> 00:02:19.431
- You like almost hit the ceiling,

00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:21.931
you were like, mmmmm, phffffs.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:28.887
- Everybody is just working
really hard to be the best at it

00:02:28.887 --> 00:02:31.414
and it's just gonna get
tougher and tougher.

00:02:31.414 --> 00:02:32.833
I take that 180 good.

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:33.816
- Yeah you did.

00:02:33.816 --> 00:02:35.678
- Flying with Sorell
now, it kinda gives me an

00:02:35.678 --> 00:02:38.028
opportunity to look at it
from a different perspective

00:02:38.028 --> 00:02:39.060
cause I can coach him.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:39.893
You ready?

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.726
- [Sorell] Mmhmm.

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.538
- Go for it.

00:02:42.538 --> 00:02:43.999
(high pitched motors whir)

00:02:43.999 --> 00:02:45.222
He's aware enough to know that

00:02:45.222 --> 00:02:46.912
he gets to do these things that

00:02:46.912 --> 00:02:48.500
most kids don't get to do.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.249
He's flying a drone, which is
this ground breaking thing.

00:02:53.249 --> 00:02:54.082
(plastic crashes)

00:02:54.082 --> 00:02:54.915
(laughter)

00:02:54.915 --> 00:02:56.441
- Dang it!

00:02:56.441 --> 00:02:57.609
We hit each other!

00:02:57.609 --> 00:02:58.442
- You hit me!

00:02:58.442 --> 00:03:00.144
What are you talking
about, "We hit each other?"

00:03:00.144 --> 00:03:00.977
You know as parents,

00:03:00.977 --> 00:03:02.947
we don't always feel like we do enough.

00:03:02.947 --> 00:03:04.630
I brought him into drone racing and

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.279
he knows he’s lucky and
he knows he's fortunate.

00:03:07.279 --> 00:03:09.058
Yeah kiddo, you were goin' pretty quick.

00:03:09.058 --> 00:03:13.275
And you know, he's grateful
for everything that he gets.

00:03:13.275 --> 00:03:16.608
(electronic beat music)

